{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790986805,"nonce":"rPW89lEzEMYWPuOiq2WTA/m2DMM=","title":"A failed cast inside try aborts under interp and hybrid instead of being caught","message":"A cast that fails at runtime inside a `try` should raise an exception the `catch` takes. Under `--mode jit` it does. Under interp and hybrid (the default), Ash aborts the process:\n\n```\nhlp_throw called without active trap; aborting\n=== CRASH: SIGABRT ...\n```\n\nNative frames from the crash: `ash_interp::...::op_safe_cast` → `hlp_dyn_castp` → `ash_std::cast::invalid_cast` → `hlp_error` → `ash_std::error::throw_impl` → `std::process::abort`.\n\nSo the error raised from the safe-cast path does not see the interpreter's active trap, even though the surrounding Haxe `try` is live; the JIT path has it.\n\n**Reproducer** (ashui `tests/fixtures/ash/cast_in_try/run.sh`, about 15 lines of Haxe):\n\n```haxe\nclass Box { public function new() {} }\nclass Trap {\n\tstatic function check(v:Dynamic, t:Dynamic):Bool return Std.isOfType(v, t);\n\tstatic function main() {\n\t\ttry {\n\t\t\tSys.println(\"isOfType: \" + check(new Box(), 3));\n\t\t} catch (e:Dynamic) {\n\t\t\tSys.println(\"caught: \" + e);\n\t\t}\n\t\tSys.println(\"after\");\n\t}\n}\n```\n\n| Mode | Output |\n|---|---|\n| expected, every mode | `caught: Can't cast i32 to hl.BaseType` then `after` |\n| jit | as expected |\n| interp | abort |\n| hybrid | abort |\n\n**How ashui hit it:** a Haxe bug of ours passed an enum abstract value where a class belonged (`Std.isOfType(x, CornerRadius)` with `PropertyId.CornerRadius` in scope). Under the default mode that crashed the process instead of raising a catchable error, which hid the real message. Only `--mode jit` showed it.\n\nFound at ash 1def0ce, macOS arm64.","files":null}]}